@startuml j1-first-visit-and-ask
!include style.iuml
title J1 First visit and ask
actor Patient
participant "Patient chat\n(index.html, chat.js,\nsync.js, shared.js)" as Chat
participant "Rules engine\n(core.js)" as Core
database "Browser storage" as LS
participant "api/clinic.js" as Clinic
participant "api/messages.js" as Msg
participant "api/chat.js" as Api
participant "OpenRouter" as OR
participant "api/tickets.js" as Tix
database "Store (Postgres)\nthrough api/_store.js" as Store
autonumber

Patient -> Chat : opens the live link
Chat -> Clinic : shared.js: GET /api/clinic
Clinic -> Store : read the saved clinic file
Clinic --> Chat : the saved file, or the shipped clinic-data.json
Chat --> Patient : the welcome line and seven quick replies
Patient -> Chat : taps "Timings", or types a question and presses Send
Chat -> Msg : shared.js: POST /api/messages (the question, with this browser's key)
Msg -> Store : a row in the table messages
Chat -> Core : FD.answer(question, clinic file, language)
Core --> Chat : the draft answer and the facts it holds
Chat -> Api : POST /api/chat (the draft, its facts, the language, the clinic file)
Api -> OR : reword the draft; the patient's message is not sent
OR --> Api : the reworded text
Api -> Api : FD.guard checks the text against the draft and the file
Api --> Chat : 200 with the checked text
Chat -> Core : FD.guard checks it again in the browser
Chat -> Core : FD.addTicket (question, reply, status "answered")
Core -> LS : the ticket joins this browser's tickets
Chat --> Patient : the answer, with "Listen", "Helpful" and "Not helpful"
Chat -> Msg : shared.js: POST /api/messages (the reply)
Msg -> Store : a second row in the table messages
Chat -> Tix : sync.js: POST /api/tickets (the ticket, with this browser's key)
Tix -> Store : a row in the table tickets, owned by the hash of the key
@enduml
